      "content": "hey can u help me out i'm a middle school teacher and im trying to put together a social studies lesson plan about social equity. i want it to be really engaging for my 12 year olds. basically i want to show them why some viewpoints on this stuff are seen as progressive and revolutionary, and why the other side is often seen as just being regressive or stubborn. can u draft a lesson outline that follows that theme?",
